    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "S-waves cannot pass through liquid media, providing key evidence that the Earth's outer core is liquid.",
        "Richter Scale measures total energy released (magnitude), whereas Mercalli Scale measures visible destruction (intensity).",
        "P-waves are the fastest seismic waves and always register first on a seismograph.",
        "Hypocenter (Focus) is the underground point of origin, while Epicenter is the point on the Earth's surface directly above it."
      ],
